{
  "schema": 1,
  "title": "The change since the last reading, one rule on every Sugar Sense surface: the partner is the reading about five minutes back whatever the sensor's cadence, a gap of more than 20 minutes shows no change, and a flat pair shows zero. The display runs these cases in tools/host_test.py.",
  "constants": {
    "windowSeconds": 270,
    "maxGapSeconds": 1200,
    "mgdlToMmol": 0.0555,
    "minusGlyph": "−",
    "flatMgdl": "0",
    "flatMmol": "0.0"
  },
  "notes": [
    "points are oldest first; ageSec is seconds before the NEWEST point (the newest has 0); mgdl is the raw reading.",
    "partner: among the points strictly older than the newest, the NEWEST one at least windowSeconds older (a Dexcom stream's previous reading, 300 s, qualifies, so nothing changes there), else the OLDEST one within maxGapSeconds (a stream only minutes old: the best span there is); null when the nearest older point is past maxGapSeconds (a sensor swap or a signal gap is not a change) or when nothing older exists (a copy of the newest point is never a partner).",
    "text: the mg/dL difference newest minus partner, converted to the display unit (times mgdlToMmol for mmol/L), rounded half away from zero (mg/dL to an integer, mmol/L to one decimal), '+' or the minus glyph, a flat pair is flatMgdl / flatMmol, never blank; null without a partner."
  ],
